s.t:
Identify and deliver cost savings and performance improvements through implementing global sourcing strategies. The primary focus for this individual will be global programmes, with stakeholders across multiple regions and offices;
Lead strategic procurement sourcing projects, end to end; with the following projects currently due to commence over the next 12 months: real estate, marketing and brand, finance transformation and client management;
Act as a procurement subject matter expert across their area/s;
Collaborate with the Procurement team and their stakeholders;
Negotiate commercial and contract terms with suppliers;
Support initiatives to ensure growing compliance and adherence to global procurement policies.

Qualified to degree level, MCIPS or a recognised procurement qualification is desirable;
Experience identifying and delivering large cost savings and efficiency opportunities through developing global sourcing strategies;
Ability to work with and influence global internal and external stakeholders;
Ability to articulate complex projects and agreement to the highest level;
experience leading large, complex global procurement projects;
Experience presenting to senior leadership teams and project committees;
A strong understanding of Procurement best practice, process and tools and its application to a comparable organization;
Excellent written, verbal skills and interpersonal skills;
Strong multitasking and organisational skills.
